<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28504" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕlissus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μέλισσος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> (Also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕlisseus</span></b> , = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μελισσεύς</span>.) <i>A king of Crete, father
				of Melissa and Amalthea</i>, <i><span class="en">Lact. 1,
				22, 19</span></i>; ib. § 28.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A grammarian and comic poet, librarian to
			Augustus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 4, 16, 30</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Suet. Gram.
			21</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A philosopher of Samos</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 37, 118</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
